<title>POLAND: POLAND'S HUTMEN TREASURY SHARES OVERSUBSCRIBED.</title>
<headline>POLAND'S HUTMEN TREASURY SHARES OVERSUBSCRIBED.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The offering of treasury's shares</p>
<p>in Poland's non-ferrous metals products maker was</p>
<p>oversubscribed, deputy treasury minister said on Thursday.</p>
<p>PAP quoted Piotr Czyzewski as saying that investors bid for</p>
<p>3,840,305 shares against 1,979,224 shares offered.</p>
<p>He said that Hutmen shares were assigned at a minimum price</p>
<p>of 30 zlotys.</p>
<p>Those who bid above the price limit had their orders</p>
<p>executed in full, while the orders at 30 zlotys were reduced by</p>
<p>85.3 percent, PAP said.</p>
<p>Hutmen is also offering 370,000 shares in employee and open</p>
<p>tranches beginning from mid-June.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
